:: Start [start] {"title":"01 / The House at the End of Night","layout":{"column":"reading","accent":"amber"}}
@action prepareTea() {
  @do $hasTea = true;
  @do $hasKey = true;
  @do $warmth += 1;
  @do $log.push({id: $log.length, text: "Mara poured two cups of tea, though only one chair was occupied."});
}

# The House at the End of Night

@ChapterMark("I", "A light where no light should be")

At the northernmost edge of the map, where the road thins into a pencil line and
then politely gives up, there is a house with one square window lit gold.

You arrive after midnight carrying rain on your coat and a letter addressed only to
**{{ $player.name }}**. The handwriting is yours. You do not remember writing it.

::: dialogue {.dialogue speaker="Mara Bell" mood="kind"}
“Come in. Wipe your feet. Whatever followed you through the constellations can wait
on the porch until we have tea.”
:::

Mara, the house's keeper, sets a blue kettle on the stove. Above it hangs a row of
keys. One is warm brass; its teeth resemble a tiny skyline.

@if (!$hasTea) {
  The kettle begins to whistle in a language that sounds almost like your childhood
  name.

  [[Steep the midnight tea => prepareTea]]
} @else {
  ::: discovery {.discovery}
  The tea tastes of smoke, honey, and the safe part of being lost. Mara slips the
  **brass key** under your saucer. “For the door that pretends to be a wall.”
  :::
}

