:: Observatory {"title":"04 / The Listening Room"}
@action tuneSignal() {
  @do $signal += 1;
  @do $insight += 1;
  @do $log.push({id: $log.length, text: "You tuned the radio one breath closer to the voice between stars."});
}

@action makePromise() {
  @do $promise = true;
  @do $warmth += 1;
  @do $log.push({id: $log.length, text: "You promised that no guest of the house would be left outside."});
}

# A sky too close to the glass

@ChapterMark("IV", "The listening room")

The observatory is smaller than it looked from below. A red blanket covers the
chair. A plate waits with three sugared biscuits. Beyond the round window, the
universe leans near enough to fog the pane.

In the radio's green eye, something vast and lonely turns in its sleep.

::: meter {.night-meter}
SIGNAL: **{{ $signal }} / 3**
:::

@if ($signal < 3) {
  Each careful adjustment separates one voice from the static: a low, frightened
  humming from outside the shape of the world.

  [[Turn the silver dial => tuneSignal]]
} @else {
  ::: dialogue {.dialogue speaker="The Far Guest" mood="small"}
  “I saw your window. I thought it was a star. May I sit beside it until morning?”
  :::
}

@if ($signal >= 3 && !$promise) {
  [[Promise it a place by the stove => makePromise]]
}

@if ($promise) {
  The house settles around your promise. Somewhere downstairs, Mara puts another
  cup on the table.

  [[Open the little door in the telescope -> WelcomeEnding]]
} @else {
  [[Close the shutters and keep the old watch -> VigilEnding]]
}

[[Read the field notes before deciding -> FieldNotes]]

