:: WelcomeEnding {"title":"05 / A Place at the Table"}
@do $ending = "welcome";
# Morning, eventually

@ChapterMark("V", "A place at the table")

You turn the telescope's small key. The door opens inward onto a darkness full of
slow eyes. For one long moment, the whole sky considers the size of the room.

Then it makes itself smaller.

By dawn, something with too many elbows is folded politely into Mara's best chair,
warming its hands around a blue cup. The stars return to their proper distance.
They seem less hungry now.

::: ending-card {.ending-card}
**THE HOUSE KEEPS ONE MORE LIGHT**

You chose hospitality over certainty. The night will remember.
:::

[[Read what the night recorded -> FieldNotes]]

[[Begin another night -> Start]]

:: VigilEnding {"title":"05 / The Kindly Watch"}
@do $ending = "vigil";
# Some doors are blankets

@ChapterMark("V", "The kindly watch")

You close the shutters, but you do not switch off the lamp. Through the wood comes
a slow scratching, then a softer sound—the Far Guest settling against the outside
wall where the bricks are warm.

You and Mara keep watch until a pale imitation of morning. Neither of you speaks.
Neither of you is alone.

::: ending-card {.ending-card}
**THE LIGHT REMAINS IN THE WINDOW**

You chose a careful kindness. The night will return when you are ready.
:::

[[Read what the night recorded -> FieldNotes]]

[[Begin another night -> Start]]
